/**
 * urdu-levels.ts
 *
 * Pre-written exercise variant pools for all 16 Urdu Learn levels.
 *
 * Every string is composed ONLY from characters produced by the verified
 * client-side phonetic map (client/src/utils/urduPhonetic.ts) so the drills are
 * actually typeable on the Urdu (CRULP-style) phonetic layout:
 *
 *   Lowercase keys  → ا ب چ ع ف گ ح ی ج ک ل م ن ہ پ ق ر س ت ء ط و ش ے ز
 *   Uppercase keys  → آ ث ڈ غ ھ ض خ ں ۃ ص ٹ ئ ظ ژ ذ
 *   Digits          → ۰ ۱ ۲ ۳ ۴ ۵ ۶ ۷ ۸ ۹ (rendered as Urdu numerals in the
 *                     Learn course via the engine's `urduNumerals` option)
 *   Punctuation     → . = ۔   , = ،   ; = ؛   ? = ؟   : = :   ! = !
 *
 * Every exercise carries exactly THREE genuinely distinct drill variants of
 * comparable difficulty; characters are introduced cumulatively so no level
 * ever uses a letter the learner has not yet met. Western digits never appear:
 * all numeric content uses Urdu numerals ۰-۹.
 *
 * Structure: URDU_VARIANTS[lessonOrder][exerciseOrder] → string[]
 * Both dimensions are 1-indexed, matching the English VARIANTS registry.
 */

